 ],
 "drivingQuestion": "Is there a case where eating any amount incurs liability?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "All apparent exceptions are answered; the Rabbis' claim stands.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": "shevuot.sugya072",
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shevuot.21b.15",
   "daf": "21b",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "וַהֲרֵי הֶקְדֵּשׁ! הָא בָּעֵינַן שָׁוֶה פְּרוּטָה.",
   "en": "The Gemara asks: «But isn’t» one who eats less than an olive-bulk of «consecrated» food liable? The Gemara answers: In order to be liable for eating consecrated food, «we require» a different measure, an amount «worth one peruta.» One is not liable for eating an amount worth less than that."
  },
  {
   "id": "shevuot.21b.16",
   "daf": "21b",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "וַהֲרֵי מְפָרֵשׁ! מְפָרֵשׁ נָמֵי כִּבְרִיָּה דָּמֵי.",
   "en": "The Gemara asks: «But isn’t» one who «specifies» in his oath that he is prohibited from eating any amount liable for doing so? The Gemara answers: One who «specifies» that eating any amount is prohibited is «indeed comparable to» one who eats a whole «entity,» since he has granted it significance."
  },
  {
   "id": "shevuot.21b.17",
   "daf": "21b",
   "sentenceId": 16,
   "he": "וַהֲרֵי עָפָר! אֶלָּא",
   "en": "The Gemara asks: «But isn’t» there an unresolved question with regard to one who took an oath not to eat and then ate «dirt?» If, as the Rabbis claim, one is not liable for eating less than a full measure, you could «rather»"
  },
  {
   "id": "shevuot.22a.1",
   "daf": "22a",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "תִּיפְשׁוֹט דְּבָעֵי רָבָא: ״שְׁבוּעָה שֶׁלֹּא אוֹכַל״ וְאָכַל עָפָר, בְּכַמָּה? תִּפְשׁוֹט עַד דְּאִיכָּא כְּזַיִת! כִּי קָאָמְרִינַן – בְּמִידֵּי דְּבַר אֲכִילָה קָאָמְרִינַן.",
   "en": "«answer that» which «Rava asks» with regard to one who says: On my «oath I will not eat, and» who then «ate dirt.» Rava’s question is: «How much» must he eat «in» order to be liable? Based on the Rabbis’ statement, «you could answer» that he is not liable «unless there is an olive-bulk» that he has eaten. The Gemara rejects this conclusion: «When we say» in the mishna that there are no cases where a person who eats less than a full measure is liable, «we say» it «with regard to items that are edible.»"
  },
  {
   "id": "shevuot.22a.2",
   "daf": "22a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "וַהֲרֵי קוּנָּמוֹת! קוּנָּמוֹת נָמֵי כִּמְפָרֵשׁ דָּמֵי.",
   "en": "The Gemara asks: «But aren’t konamot» an example of a case where one is liable for eating even less than an olive-bulk? The Gemara answers: «Konamot are also like» a case where he «specifies» that any amount is forbidden for consumption."
  }
 ],
